{"code": "20261112T112427.697095-b874d7", "file": "sassa2005", "line": 13, "text": "Mention that the paper defines Um as w and in your text only use the standard notation we use as in Umax, not w/Ueta\n\nalso, this data is from hotwire aneometry so the coordlength distribution should be applied, similar as to belin and mouri, y is ~3 time higher and Rmax islower. *there should be a write of of the coordlenght method some where in the paper? refer to it here and apply correction. also the paper has 7 points 2 of which clearly dont fit (the st1,2 datapoints). I note that the std hotwire anemometry appears to give data that sits closer to our curve then the mouri2009 data. this is awkward. multipying it with the same constant would give too high U values\n\nnote that there is also a probability function of d/eta on a linear scale, and this should be added to the data on the distribution and fitted with the two lognormals *see fig 3)", "who": "flm", "ts": "2026-11-12T11:48:41"}
